@startuml
title RuleSphere - Promote, Rollback and Synchronize Fleet\nUC-18..20, UC-27
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #177E8D
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF6F8

actor "Release Manager / Authorized Operator" as User
boundary "Management API" as API
participant AuthorizationService as Auth
participant DesiredActiveState as Desired
database "Immutable Audit Evidence" as Audit
participant DistributionService as Distribution
database "Artifact Store" as Artifacts
participant "RuntimeNode (each active node)" as Node
participant FleetConvergenceView as Fleet

' Phase 1: Promote / Rollback Request
User -> API: Promote candidate / Roll back to prior version
activate API

API -> Auth: authorize(user, operation, scope)
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Access decision
deactivate Auth

break Unauthorized
  API --> User: Access denied
end

API -> Desired: Check target eligibility and release policy
activate Desired

break Target ineligible
  Desired --> API: Reject operation
  API --> User: Policy error
end

API -> Desired: Switch desired Active pointer to target artifact
Desired -> Audit: Record actor, from/to version, timestamp, reason
activate Audit
Audit --> Desired: Logged
deactivate Audit

Desired -> Distribution: Publish desired state change
activate Distribution
Distribution -> Fleet: Record desired version and event emission time
activate Fleet
Fleet --> Distribution: Recorded
deactivate Fleet

Desired --> API: Desired state committed
deactivate Desired

API --> User: Desired state updated; fleet convergence pending
deactivate API

' Phase 2: Per-Node Concurrent Synchronization
loop Each active Runtime node
  Distribution ->> Node: Desired state notification
  activate Node
  Node -> Artifacts: Fetch exact immutable artifact and dependencies
  activate Artifacts
  Artifacts --> Node: Artifact and integrity/version metadata
  deactivate Artifacts
  Node -> Node: Verify integrity; load and validate complete snapshot
  alt Load succeeds
    Node -> Node: Make snapshot eligible for new requests
    Node ->> Fleet: Report loaded version, eligibility and health
  else Fetch / integrity / load failure
    Node ->> Fleet: Report load error and non-converged state
    note right of Node
      Never serve failed artifact.
      Continue with already-loaded eligible artifacts (FR-DIST-004).
      Retry/reconciliation strategy requires ADR.
    end note
  end
  deactivate Node
end
deactivate Distribution

note over Distribution,Fleet
  SLA (NFR-CONS-001): 100% of active nodes loaded/eligible within <=2s
  of publication-event emission; surface any lag or breach.
  In-flight executions retain their original atomic snapshot.
  Rollback reuses a prior artifact; no cloning or node restart.
end note

' Phase 3: Observe Convergence
User -> API: Observe convergence
activate API

API -> Auth: authorize(user, observe fleet, scope)
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Access decision
deactivate Auth

alt Authorized
  API -> Fleet: Get scoped desired / loaded state per node
  activate Fleet
  Fleet --> API: Versions, last observation, health, lag and errors
  deactivate Fleet
  API --> User: Fleet convergence view
else Unauthorized
  API --> User: Access denied
end
deactivate API

@enduml
